prompt.text:
Implement a self-contained TypeScript ledger-report module.

Export these declarations:

```ts
export interface LedgerEntry {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly account: string;
  readonly day: number;
  readonly delta: number;
}

export interface LedgerReport {
  readonly startDay: number;
  readonly endDay: number;
  readonly accounts: string[];
  readonly openingBalances: Record<string, number>;
  readonly closingBalances: Record<string, number>;
  readonly entries: LedgerEntry[];
}

export function createLedgerReport(
  accountsText: string,
  startDay: number,
  endDay: number,
  source: readonly LedgerEntry[],
): LedgerReport;
```

Parse `accountsText` as comma-separated identifiers, trimming whitespace, discarding empty pieces, and removing duplicates while preserving first occurrence order. Every retained identifier must match `/^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_-]{0,15}$/`; otherwise throw `RangeError`. `startDay`, `endDay`, and every entry day must be integers, `startDay` must not exceed `endDay`, every delta must be finite, and every entry ID and account must satisfy the same identifier rule. Invalid data must throw `RangeError`, even when an entry belongs to an unselected account.

For each selected account, the opening balance is the sum of deltas on days strictly before `startDay`; the closing balance is the sum on days up to and including `endDay`. Returned entries include selected accounts on the inclusive date range. Order them by day, then ID, retaining source order when both compare equally. Empty account input produces empty balances and entries after source validation. Do not mutate the input or alias returned entries with source objects.

Return only the complete source file; do not include Markdown fences or prose.

